{title: Hallelujah! What a Savior}
{artist: Philip Bliss}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 69}

Verse 1
"Man of [Bb]sorrows," what a [Eb]name for the [Bb]Son of [F]God, who [Bb]came
ruined [Eb]sinners [Bb]to re[Gm]claim! Halle[Bb]lujah! [F]What a [Bb]Savior!

Verse 2
Bearing shame and scoffing rude,
In my place condemned He stood;
Sealed my pardon with His blood. Hallelujah! What a Savior!

Verse 3
Guilty, vile, and helpless we;
Spotless Lamb of God was He;
"Full atonement!" can it be? Hallelujah! What a Savior!

Verse 4
Lifted up was He to die;
"It is finished!" was His cry;
Now in Heav'n exalted high. Hallelujah! What a Savior!

Verse 5
When He comes, our glorious King,
All His ransomed home to bring,
Then anew His song we'll sing: Hallelujah! What a Savior!
